<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Canonical origin set 2026-09-05: https://krzysztof-tarka.netlify.app

  Every <loc> used a REPLACE-WITH-CANONICAL-ORIGIN.invalid placeholder until then, because the
  Netlify site did not exist. An XML file has no runtime, so unlike SeoService's canonical —
  which reads document.location.origin and was always correct — this advertised URLs that
  could not resolve to anything that read it.

  No custom domain is planned. If one arrives, changing the origin here is part of a site
  move rather than an edit: 301 from the old host and a change of address in Search Console.

  Scope: static public routes only. Project detail pages (/projects/:id) are deliberately
  absent — their URLs are UUIDs known only at runtime, and this is a build-time artifact in
  `frontend/public/`, which Netlify copies verbatim. Listing them needs either a build-time
  API call or a generation step, and the 2026-08-10 SEO ADR in docs/DECISIONS.md defers that
  alongside prerendering, for the same reason: it would make the Netlify build depend on the
  VPS backend, which the committed API client exists to avoid.

  Admin routes are omitted on purpose; robots.txt disallows them.

  No <lastmod>: a hardcoded date would be wrong the moment anything changes, and there is no
  build step here to generate a real one. An absent lastmod is honest; a stale one is a lie
  crawlers act on.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://krzysztof-tarka.netlify.app/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://krzysztof-tarka.netlify.app/contact</loc>
    <changefreq>yearly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.5</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
